msgid "Python reference counts (:func:`sys.getrefcount`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/heap-introspection-apis.rst:39
msgid ":mod:`tracemalloc` module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/heap-introspection-apis.rst:40
msgid "Python's :mod:`gc` stats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/heap-introspection-apis.rst:41
msgid ""
":term:`RSS`, :term:`VMS` or :term:`USS` due to allocator caching, especially "
"for small objects. This can happen, for example, when you forget to "
"``Py_DECREF`` a Python object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../blog/2025/heap-introspection-apis.rst:45
msgid ""
"psutil's new functions let you query the allocator (e.g. glibc) directly, "
